        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: عاجل",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عاجل — ʿājil — \"urgent; breaking news\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قطع التلفاز البرنامج لخبر عاجل. qaṭaʿa at-tilfāz al-barnāmaj li-khabar ʿājil. The television interrupted the programme for breaking news."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "خبر عاجل (ʿājil): breaking news."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عاجل (ʿājil) is built on the native Arabic root ʿ-j-l (Lane), \"to hasten\", the root of the taught mustaʿjil, in a hurry. ʿĀjil is \"what comes quickly\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
